\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, in the fullness of my might,
\par I would for Thee be strong:
\par While runneth o'er each dear delight,
\par To Thee should soar  my song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I would not give the world my heart,
\par And then profess Thy love;
\par I would not feel my strength depart,
\par And then Thy service prove.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I would not with swift-winged zeal
\par On the world's errands go,
\par And labour up the heavenly hill
\par With weary feet and slow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O not for Thee my weak desires,
\par My poorer, baser part!
\par O not for Thee my fading fires,
\par The ashes of my heart!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O choose me in my golden time,
\par In my dear joys have part!
\par For Thee the glory of my prime,
\par The fullness of my heart!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I cannot, Lord, too early take
\par The convenant divine;
\par O ne'er the happy heart may break
\par Whose earliest love was Thine!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

